  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nThe last gasp of frontal and shortwave movement SE of Pittsburgh\nwill push lingering showers/thunderstorms out of the region by\nsunset. Cool, dry advection plus the loss of diurnal heating\nends most precipitation chances tonight, save for weak\nconvergence along the higher terrain that could squeeze a brief,\nlocalized light rain shower overnight.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nThe upper pattern features a closed upper trough meandering over\nthe New England region late tonight through Thursday. Weak\nshortwave movement around this low plus wrap-around moisture\ncould foster isolated to scattered diurnal storms Wednesday\n(east of I-77) and Thursday (mainly along higher terrain) in\nwhat otherwise would be a drying period with slowly building\nhigh pressure.\n\nThese storms are unlikely to pose risks due to limited\ninstability (less than 500 J/kg).",
